infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title ORM eager loading vs DataLoader: when each wins
  desc The deciding question — do you know at one place in code what all the data needs are?
  compares
    - label ORM eager loading
      children
        - label Use when the shape is known at the query site
          desc One .includes / select_related / joinedload, declared up front
        - label ORM picks JOIN or IN and runs it upfront
          desc Concentrated at a single query construction site
        - label Simpler and faster for known-shape queries
          desc No async batch machinery, no request-scope cache
        - label Cannot help a GraphQL resolver tree
          desc No single site to declare 50 scattered author lookups
    - label DataLoader
      children
        - label Use when needs are scattered across code paths
          desc load(id) from any module, with no coordination
        - label One query per type — even four levels deep
          desc From 1 + N + (N x M) queries down to ~4 per request
        - label Batches on the next event-loop tick
          desc Queues IDs, fires one SELECT ... WHERE id IN (...)
        - label Request-scope cache, ~1 ms batch window
          desc p99 ~1.4 s to ~150 ms on a typical four-level query
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
